        {
            "result": "Cycle-type classification",
            "required_terms": ["same cycle lengths", "define", "tau"],
            "body": r"Conjugation relabels every cycle, so conjugate permutations have the same cycle lengths with the same multiplicities. Conversely, suppose (\sigma) and (\rho) have the same cycle type. Pair their cycles of each length, choose corresponding starting points, and define a permutation (\tau) by sending the (j)-th entry of each cycle of (\sigma) to the (j)-th entry of the paired cycle of (\rho). Send fixed points bijectively to fixed points. The cycle-relabeling formula then gives (\tau\sigma\tau^{-1}=\rho). Thus equality of cycle type is both necessary and sufficient.",
        },
